# Files Git should ignore in the Django project (not upload to GitHub)

# The database: it will hold the visitors' names and email addresses (personal data),
# so it must not be public. It is made with: python manage.py migrate
db.sqlite3

# Files Python makes by itself to start faster
__pycache__/

# The documents the website sends by email (e.g. the manifesto PDF) are shared on request only,
# so they are not uploaded. Only the README that lists them is.
front_page/files/*
!front_page/files/README.md

# While testing, emails are saved as files here instead of being sent (see MAILERS in
# config/settings.py). They contain people's names and emails, so they are not uploaded.
sent_emails/

# The private settings (the email account and its password). .env.example shows what goes in it.
.env
